East Cushitic languages are a branch of the Cushitic family spoken in the highlands of southern Ethiopia, in and around the Rift Valley.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/higo-province"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/higo-province.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Higo Province</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Higo Province was an old province of Japan in central Kyushu, corresponding to modern Kumamoto Prefecture.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hiiumaa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hiiumaa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hiiumaa</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Hiiumaa is the second-largest island of Estonia, lying in the Baltic Sea north of Saaremaa, and known in German and Swedish as Dagö.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hijikata-toshizo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hijikata-toshizo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hijikata Toshizō</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hijikata Toshizō was a Japanese swordsman and vice-commander of the Shinsengumi, the special police force that defended the shogunate in Kyoto in the 1860s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/hijra"><span class="enc-name">Hijra</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Hijra was the migration of the Prophet Muhammad and his followers from Mecca to Medina in 622 CE, which marks the start of the Islamic calendar.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/hijra-of-usman-dan-fodio"><span class="enc-name">Hijra of Usman dan Fodio</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Hijra of Usman dan Fodio was the migration of the reform